        "original_id": "14746bf2-1704-5d3f-a905-cb7a85e00fc4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lisa Raymond, Liezel Huber, Cara Black, Bob Bryan, Nadia Petrova, Meghann Shaughnessy, Rennae Stubbs\n- Events: 2005 NASDAQ-100 Open – Women's Doubles\n- Topics: Grand Slam titles, women's doubles, mixed doubles, tennis partnerships\n\nFacts:\n- Lisa Raymond has won 11 Grand Slam titles, including 6 in women's doubles and 5 in mixed doubles.\n- Liezel Huber, née Horn, was born on 21 August 1976 and is a retired South African-American tennis player who represented the United States internationally.\n- Liezel Huber won four Grand Slam women's doubles titles with Cara Black, one Grand Slam women's doubles title with Lisa Raymond, and two Grand Slam mixed doubles titles with Bob Bryan.\n- At the 2005 NASDAQ-100 Open – Women's Doubles, defending champions Nadia Petrova and Meghann Shaughnessy lost in the quarterfinals to Lisa Raymond and Rennae Stubbs.",
